<mxGraphModel><root><mxCell id="0"/><mxCell id="1" parent="0"/><mxCell id="2" parent="1" style="rounded=0;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=6;fontSize=14;whiteSpace=wrap;resizeHeight=1;autosize=0;fixedWidth=1;" value="&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;LaminarFlow-Backend/internal/migrate/runner.go&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1"><mxGeometry height="30" width="700" y="260" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="3" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;fontSize=14;resizeHeight=1;autosize=0;fixedWidth=1;" value="&lt;div&gt;&lt;font&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Andale Mono&quot;&gt;package migrate&lt;/font&gt; — &lt;font face=&quot;Andale Mono&quot;&gt;+ Pending&lt;/font&gt; is exported; main.go calls it at startup, before it begins serving&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Helvetica&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;the whole body is one &lt;a href=&quot;#func#withLock&quot;&gt;withLock&lt;/a&gt; closure — Up&#39;s loop with the &lt;a href=&quot;#func#apply&quot;&gt;apply&lt;/a&gt; step removed, so the two can never disagree&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1"><mxGeometry height="40" width="700" y="290" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="4" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;fontFamily=Andale Mono;fontSize=14;resizeHeight=1;autosize=0;fixedWidth=1;" value="&lt;div&gt;&lt;font&gt;func &lt;b&gt;Pending(&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;ctx context.Context&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;pool *pgxpool.Pool&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;migrations []&lt;a href=&quot;#class#Migration&quot;&gt;Migration&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font&gt;&lt;b&gt;)&lt;/b&gt; ([]Migration, error)&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1"><mxGeometry height="100" width="700" y="330" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="5" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;fontSize=14;resizeHeight=1;autosize=0;fixedWidth=1;" value="&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;Returns the migrations Up would apply, oldest first — an empty slice and a nil error when the database is already up to date.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;The error means the lock or the schema_migrations read failed, so whether the schema matches is unknown; main.go treats that&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;as fatal rather than serving anyway.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1"><mxGeometry height="60" width="700" y="430" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="6" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;fontFamily=Andale Mono;fontSize=14;resizeHeight=1;autosize=0;fixedWidth=1;" value="&lt;div&gt;&lt;font&gt;-&amp;gt; return pending, err&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1"><mxGeometry height="30" width="700" y="490" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="7" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;fontFamily=Andale Mono;fontSize=14;resizeHeight=1;autosize=0;fixedWidth=1;" value="&lt;div&gt;&lt;font&gt;{&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;var pending []&lt;a href=&quot;#class#Migration&quot;&gt;Migration&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;err := &lt;a href=&quot;#func#withLock&quot;&gt;withLock&lt;/a&gt;(ctx, pool, func(ctx context.Context, conn *pgxpool.Conn) error {&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;applied, err := &lt;a href=&quot;#func#appliedVersions&quot;&gt;appliedVersions&lt;/a&gt;(ctx, conn)&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;if err != nil {&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;return err&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;}&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;for _, m := range migrations {&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;if !applied[m.Version] {&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;pending = append(pending, m)&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;}&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;}&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;return nil&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;})&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;return pending, err&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font&gt;}&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Helvetica&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;main.go uses this to refuse to serve against a schema it does not match, rather than failing later on the first query that&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Helvetica&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;hits a missing column — a startup that stops loudly is cheaper to diagnose than one request in twenty failing&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1"><mxGeometry height="420" width="700" y="520" as="geometry"/></mxCell></root></mxGraphModel>
